<title>USA: Anheuser-Busch sells $250 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Anheuser-Busch sells $250 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Anheuser-Busch Cos Inc was priced on Friday in the U.S. high-grade bond market via lead underwriter JP Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Anheuser-Busch holds a leading market position in the U.S. beer industry.</p>
<p>BORROWER ANHEUSER-BUSCH COS INC</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	   COUPON 7.10	  MATURITY 6/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	     ISS PRICE 99.921   FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1	YIELD 7.111	  PAY FREQ  SEMI</p>
<p>S&amp;P A-PLUS	     SPREAD 55 BPS	CALLABLE SEVEN YEARS</p>
<p>(( Corporate bond unit, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
